    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "The present application under Section 528 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita has been filed to modify the impugned order dated 25.03.2025 passed by Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Ist,\nSaharanpur in Misc. Case No. 770 of 2024, arising out of Case Crime No. 309 of 2024, under Smt Alina vs State Of U.P. And 2 Others on 5 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/74511304/\n1 Sections 376 of I.P.C., Police Station- Kotwali Dehat, District- Saharanpur, and not summoned the other two co-accused persons under Section 376-D of I.P.C. (in which the F.I.R. has been lodged).\nAfter some arguments, learned counsel for the applicant does not want to press this application and wants liberty to file an appropriate application/ proceedings before the court of competent jurisdiction.\nCertified copy of the order may be returned to the learned counsel for the applicant after retaining a xerox thereof.\nIn view of the above, the application is dismissed as not pressed with the aforesaid liberty.",
